Use Solaris extended privilege policies to sandbox Codex filesystem
helpers. ppriv removes file_read, file_write, and net_access globally and
restores filesystem privileges only for explicitly permitted path objects.

Solaris extended policies cannot express a broad writable directory with
nested read-only exceptions. Narrow each structured helper request to its
exact source and destination paths after checking the original Codex policy.
Reject protected metadata components explicitly, preserving .git, .codex, and
.agents paths while allowing permitted native apply_patch changes to run in
the sandbox. Keep general command execution on the existing approval path until
its richer policy can be represented without weakening the sandbox.

